A||||12||GT Bastard||Does this sound like a bad idea????||||5||
Z||000000||GT Bastard||05-01-2000||08:04 PM||||Just had a thought... A friend of mine has 4 BFG Euro T/A P245 50R15's in good shape.  They came off his old camaro.  I know they might be a little oversized, but do you think they'd rub up front?  Also, I'm running aftermarket 5-spoke rims that are 15 by 6 inches.  I've seen them on 15 by 7 inch rims, and they seem to fit quite nicely.  Would 6 inch wide rims be pushing the envelope?  Normally I would never buy tires this size, but he's offering them pretty cheap, and the ones I currently have are 195's all around(which sucks.)  thanks kiddies!||||reg||5
Z||000001||GT Bastard||05-01-2000||10:17 PM||||?||||reg||1
Z||000002||Haze_Performance||05-01-2000||10:24 PM||||My guess would be that they would rub.......Anyone else have an idea??||||reg||1
Z||000003||1FST2M6||05-01-2000||10:29 PM||||i wouldn't worry about them rubbing.. i'd be more concerned about the ride quality... with that much tire unsupported your car above like 40mph will sway on a center axis. trying to find a good point to settle on the tire.. if your hard into a corner you'll roll the tire onto the unsupported part and the car will shift and can cause you to lose control. (slip angle) odds are you'll be displeased with the lack luster handeling due to the near 2" unsupported tire.. i'd stick with no more than a 225! even that your pushing it.. the 215 are great and 205 although sound tiny with a sticky tire will WAY handle better than most people can drive... my 205s ROCK! ||||reg||1
Z||000004||1FST2M6||05-01-2000||10:32 PM||||245/25.4-6/2=1.8  (245 tire section width, 25.4 to change mm to inches, 6 width of wheel, 2 number of sided the tire actually touch the wheel.. insid and outside) 1.8 # of inches on the fender-side and exterior side f the tire that is UNsupported by the wheel.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Haze_Performance||05-01-2000||10:51 PM||||I stand corrected....||||reg||12
Z||000007||1FST2M6||05-01-2000||11:00 PM||||sorry Haze.. not correcting.. just doing math..    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  sorry about that... your right! they WON'T rub... my 245s on my 17x8s were fine.. but they were on a ... a wider wheel. ||||reg||1
Z||000008||GT Bastard||05-01-2000||11:17 PM||||Thanks for the info 1fst...||||reg||1
Z||000009||olympic||05-02-2000||03:03 AM||||245's are waaaaay too wide for 6" rims.  they need at least 7" rims, 8" being ideal.||||reg||1
Z||000010||lowCG||05-02-2000||10:34 AM||||Yup,what Oly said,the tread would be distorted,and finding a good tire pressure could be very difficult.205 is the size for a 5.5-7" rim from my past experiences.<BR>Not saying that it wouldn't be fun to try and see how it worked though,you never know until you try...<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000011||phillip||05-02-2000||11:07 AM||||if they're cheap enough or he'll separate them just mount 2 at first and mount them in front. if they rub put them in back. if the rim fit is a problem maybe if they were cheap to you they'll be easy to sell to someone else cheap too.||||reg||1
Z||000012||87PegasusGT||05-03-2000||03:56 PM||||Will they fit ok on my 7.0" 87GT rear wheels?||||reg||1
Z||000013||batboy||05-03-2000||09:54 PM||||Yes, they'll work on a 7" wide rim, that's as small as I'd go. They probably will fit on the rear, barely. But, I'll bet money that those will rub on the front. At least during a turn and a bump at the same time. Too wide for the front even if for some miracle they didn't rub, they'll hunt and follow every seam and crack in the road. Use a pair of them as rear tires with a pair of back-ups tires. Try to find the same brand and type tires in a smaller size for the front...that's what I'd do.||||reg||1
